        "Hours imputation. For workers in the linked sample of the Survey on Labour Conditions by Employment Type, we observe monthly contractual hours directly. For other workers we impute hours as the median of contractual hours in cells defined by two-digit industry, six firm-size classes, one-digit occupation, sex, five-year age group and full-time or part-time status, computed from the survey wave closest to the reference month. In the linked sample, 93 percent of workers classified as treated using imputed hours are also classified as treated using observed hours, and the employment estimates obtained with observed hours in the linked sample are within 0.2 percentage points of those obtained with imputed hours.",
        "Wage definitions. Monthly wages are those reported for employment-insurance contributions and include basic pay and fixed allowances but exclude irregular bonuses and overtime pay, which corresponds closely to the definition of wages counted towards the minimum in 2018. Workers whose reported monthly wage implies an hourly wage more than 10 percent below the applicable minimum are excluded, because their wages are likely to be misreported or their employers non-compliant; they represent 2.4 percent of the low-wage sample.",
